WEBVTT

1
00:04:07.596 --> 00:04:09.596
It's time to get out.

2
00:07:38.806 --> 00:07:40.806
Don't bleed to death.

3
00:07:45.246 --> 00:07:47.246
- Hello, Mitchell.
- Bond.

4
00:07:47.315 --> 00:07:49.912
The Americans are gonna be
none too pleased about this.

5
00:07:49.917 --> 00:07:51.981
I promised them Le Chiffre,
and they got Le Chiffre.

6
00:07:51.986 --> 00:07:53.482
They got his body.

7
00:07:53.487 --> 00:07:55.797
If they'd wanted his
soul, they should...

8
00:07:55.802 --> 00:07:57.653
have made a deal
with a priest.

9
00:07:57.658 --> 00:08:00.024
- Has he said anything?
- No.

10
00:08:00.094 --> 00:08:02.927
I'm going to check
the perimeter, ma'am.

11
00:08:04.065 --> 00:08:05.728
You look like hell.

12
00:08:05.733 --> 00:08:08.031
When's the last
time you slept?

13
00:08:09.170 --> 00:08:11.067
Vesper's boyfriend,
Yusef Kabira,

14
00:08:11.072 --> 00:08:12.859
the one who was
abducted in Morocco,

15
00:08:12.864 --> 00:08:14.403
the one she was
trying to save.

16
00:08:14.408 --> 00:08:16.740
His body was washed up
on a beach in Ibiza.

17
00:08:16.844 --> 00:08:19.506
We're meant to believe
the fish did that to his face.

18
00:08:19.580 --> 00:08:21.444
His wallet and ID
were in his pocket.

19
00:08:21.449 --> 00:08:23.245
- Well, that's convenient.
- Quite.

20
00:08:23.250 --> 00:08:25.405
Which is why I did a
DNA check on a lock...

21
00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:27.414
of his hair found in
Vesper's apartment.

22
00:08:27.521 --> 00:08:28.684
It's not him.

23
00:08:28.689 --> 00:08:30.453
A lock of his hair?

24
00:08:30.458 --> 00:08:33.256
I wouldn't have thought
Vesper the sentimental type.

25
00:08:33.361 --> 00:08:35.535
Well, we never
really know anyone,

26
00:08:35.540 --> 00:08:37.540
do we?

27
00:08:37.632 --> 00:08:39.759
But I do need to know, Bond.

28
00:08:40.134 --> 00:08:42.762
I need to know that
I can trust you.

29
00:08:43.638 --> 00:08:44.767
And you don't?

30
00:08:44.772 --> 00:08:46.235
Well, it'd be a pretty
cold bastard...

31
00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.480
who didn't want revenge...

32
00:08:47.485 --> 00:08:49.205
for the death of
someone he loved.

33
00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.269
You don't have to
worry about me.

34
00:08:51.379 --> 00:08:54.610
I'm not gonna go chasing him.
He's not important.

35
00:08:56.884 --> 00:08:58.884
And neither was she.

36
00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:01.050
It's clear, ma'am.

37
00:09:01.055 --> 00:09:03.285
- Thanks, Mitchell.
- Shall we?

38
00:09:22.476 --> 00:09:25.104
Are you gonna tell
us who you work for?

39
00:09:25.179 --> 00:09:28.410
I was always very
interested to meet you.

40
00:09:28.482 --> 00:09:30.848
I'd heard so much
about you from Vesper.

41
00:09:30.951 --> 00:09:34.079
The real shame is that
if she hadn't killed herself,

42
00:09:34.155 --> 00:09:36.155
we would have had you, too.

43
00:09:36.157 --> 00:09:39.490
I think you would have done
anything for her.

44
00:09:39.593 --> 00:09:41.327
Well, you know you're
not in Britain,

45
00:09:41.332 --> 00:09:43.159
and God knows where
you'll be tomorrow.

46
00:09:43.164 --> 00:09:44.660
Which should tell you
that eventually...

47
00:09:44.665 --> 00:09:47.793
you will tell us about
the people you work with,

48
00:09:47.868 --> 00:09:49.434
and the longer it takes,

49
00:09:49.439 --> 00:09:51.463
the more painful
we'll make it.

50
00:09:53.808 --> 00:09:56.675
You really don't know
anything about us.

51
00:10:00.481 --> 00:10:02.113
It's so amusing because...

52
00:10:02.118 --> 00:10:04.315
we are on the other
side, thinking,

53
00:10:04.385 --> 00:10:05.310
'The Ml6, the CIA,

54
00:10:05.315 --> 00:10:07.183
they're looking
over our shoulders.

55
00:10:07.188 --> 00:10:09.051
'They're listening to
our conversations.'

56
00:10:09.056 --> 00:10:12.184
And the truth is
you don't even know we exist.

57
00:10:12.293 --> 00:10:15.729
Well, we do now, Mr. White,
and we're quick learners.

58
00:10:17.298 --> 00:10:19.298
Oh, really?

59
00:10:19.834 --> 00:10:22.163
Well, then, the first thing
you should know about us...

60
00:10:22.168 --> 00:10:24.659
is that we have
people everywhere.

61
00:10:25.505 --> 00:10:27.505
Am I right?

62
00:15:41.486 --> 00:15:43.486
Anything?

63
00:15:43.822 --> 00:15:46.313
Craig Mitchell worked for me
for eight years.

64
00:15:46.391 --> 00:15:48.143
He passed a full
security check...

65
00:15:48.148 --> 00:15:49.956
and lie detector
test every year.

66
00:15:49.961 --> 00:15:51.518
Didn't leave so much
as a scrap of...

67
00:15:51.523 --> 00:15:52.659
paper to explain any of it.

68
00:15:52.664 --> 00:15:55.633
Eight years.
Five as my personal bodyguard.

69
00:15:55.734 --> 00:15:58.131
I found this and three other
bloody Christmas presents

70
00:15:58.136 --> 00:15:59.399
I bought him about the house.

71
00:15:59.404 --> 00:16:01.404
I don't think he smoked.

72
00:16:01.506 --> 00:16:03.036
And you had to kill him.

73
00:16:03.041 --> 00:16:04.768
Couldn't bring him in
for questioning so...

74
00:16:04.773 --> 00:16:06.339
that we might actually
learn something.

75
00:16:06.344 --> 00:16:08.245
When someone says we
got people everywhere,

76
00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:09.576
you expect it to be hyperbole.

77
00:16:09.581 --> 00:16:12.573
Lots of people say that.
Florists use that expression.

78
00:16:12.684 --> 00:16:14.656
Doesn't mean that
they've got somebody...

79
00:16:14.661 --> 00:16:16.583
working for them inside
the bloody room.

80
00:16:16.588 --> 00:16:18.852
What the hell is this
organization, Bond?

81
00:16:18.924 --> 00:16:20.676
How can they be everywhere...

82
00:16:20.681 --> 00:16:22.681
and we know
nothing about them?

83
00:16:23.595 --> 00:16:26.344
- I assume we found
no trace of White.

84
00:16:26.349 --> 00:16:26.660
No.

85
00:16:26.665 --> 00:16:28.028
The agent guarding the
door in the garage...

86
00:16:28.033 --> 00:16:29.996
was dead before you passed him
on the stairs.

87
00:16:30.001 --> 00:16:31.865
I passed him on
the stairs? Christ.

88
00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:33.515
Mitchell must have
killed him when he...

89
00:16:33.520 --> 00:16:34.835
went out to check
the perimeter.

90
00:16:34.840 --> 00:16:36.603
You're lucky to be here.

91
00:16:36.608 --> 00:16:38.238
Do you think
White's still alive?

92
00:16:38.243 --> 00:16:40.107
- Yes, I do.
- What is it?

93
00:16:40.112 --> 00:16:42.075
Craig Mitchell, 45 years old.

94
00:16:42.080 --> 00:16:44.514
No living family.
Gave generously to charity.

95
00:16:44.583 --> 00:16:46.413
Tell me you know
more than that.

96
00:16:46.418 --> 00:16:47.481
Our moneymen went through...

97
00:16:47.486 --> 00:16:49.082
every bill in Mitchell's
wallet and house.

98
00:16:49.087 --> 00:16:52.113
- How much did he have?
- Less than 100 pounds,

99
00:16:52.224 --> 00:16:54.224
and about the same in
euros and dollars.

100
00:16:54.259 --> 00:16:55.856
Excuse me. Excuse me, ma'am.

101
00:16:55.861 --> 00:16:57.582
We've done a complete
forensic analysis...

102
00:16:57.587 --> 00:16:59.226
of every note and its
traceable history.

103
00:16:59.231 --> 00:17:01.231
Not in the mood.

104
00:17:02.634 --> 00:17:04.634
After you.

105
00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:05.686
This particular note from

106
00:17:05.691 --> 00:17:06.900
Mitchell's wallet
may be of interest.

107
00:17:06.905 --> 00:17:08.034
Scanning.

108
00:17:08.039 --> 00:17:09.338
We introduced
tagged bills into

109
00:17:09.343 --> 00:17:11.104
Le Chiffre's money-laundering
operation...

110
00:17:11.109 --> 00:17:13.270
by intercepting
illegal payoffs.

111
00:17:13.378 --> 00:17:14.951
We traced money
through several of...

112
00:17:14.956 --> 00:17:16.443
his bank accounts
around the world.

113
00:17:16.448 --> 00:17:17.777
That's pretty thin.

114
00:17:17.782 --> 00:17:19.079
At the rate money
changes hands,

115
00:17:19.084 --> 00:17:20.385
you could probably
find a tenner...

116
00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.281
in my wallet with a tag.

117
00:17:21.286 --> 00:17:22.018
That's true, ma'am.

118
00:17:22.023 --> 00:17:23.450
A single bill could
be a coincidence,

119
00:17:23.455 --> 00:17:25.285
but what about a whole stack?

120
00:17:25.290 --> 00:17:25.883
These bills,

121
00:17:25.888 --> 00:17:27.621
from the same series
as Mitchell's,

122
00:17:27.626 --> 00:17:30.618
were just scanned at a bank
in Port-au-Prince, Haiti,

123
00:17:30.729 --> 00:17:33.596
deposited in the
account of a Mr. Slate.

124
00:17:34.132 --> 00:17:35.395
Impress me.

125
00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.564
We have a Mr. Edmund Slate
returning to Port-au-Prince...

126
00:17:37.569 --> 00:17:39.662
from Heathrow this morning.

127
00:17:39.771 --> 00:17:42.078
His entry documents
have him staying...

128
00:17:42.083 --> 00:17:43.603
at the Hotel Dessalines.

129
00:17:43.608 --> 00:17:45.608
He's in room 325.

130
00:17:54.986 --> 00:17:57.113
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

131
00:20:05.316 --> 00:20:07.750
Do you have any
messages for 325?

132
00:20:09.920 --> 00:20:10.267
No, sir.

133
00:20:10.272 --> 00:20:12.151
The only message was
about the briefcase...

134
00:20:12.156 --> 00:20:13.752
that was delivered earlier.

135
00:20:13.757 --> 00:20:15.502
- Did you want us to
continue holding it?

136
00:20:15.507 --> 00:20:16.655
No. No, I'll take that now.

137
00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:18.660
Yes, sir.

138
00:20:21.265 --> 00:20:23.265
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

139
00:20:31.575 --> 00:20:33.405
Get in.

140
00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:35.410
- What?
- Get in.

141
00:20:37.915 --> 00:20:39.915
All right.

142
00:20:42.686 --> 00:20:43.916
You're late.

143
00:20:43.921 --> 00:20:45.946
I got pulled into a meeting.

144
00:20:46.023 --> 00:20:47.519
Who with?

145
00:20:47.524 --> 00:20:49.617
A friend of Mr. White's.

146
00:20:50.361 --> 00:20:52.488
Don't think I know him.

147
00:20:56.300 --> 00:20:57.496
It's funny.

148
00:20:57.501 --> 00:20:59.501
You don't look at
all like I expected.

149
00:20:59.803 --> 00:21:01.803
Really? What were
you expecting?

150
00:21:01.839 --> 00:21:04.307
I didn't think
geologists looked so...

151
00:21:04.375 --> 00:21:06.375
So?

152
00:21:08.846 --> 00:21:10.846
A friend of yours?

153
00:21:10.948 --> 00:21:12.973
I don't have any friends.

154
00:21:19.990 --> 00:21:22.288
Get out of the way. Move.

155
00:21:34.171 --> 00:21:36.171
We didn't settle on a price.

156
00:21:36.173 --> 00:21:38.173
Make me an offer.

157
00:21:38.909 --> 00:21:41.571
We can work it out
later, over drinks.

158
00:21:45.182 --> 00:21:46.628
Dominic didn't give
you any trouble,

159
00:21:46.633 --> 00:21:46.912
did he?

160
00:21:46.917 --> 00:21:48.917
No.

161
00:21:52.656 --> 00:21:54.656
What the hell is this?

162
00:21:54.658 --> 00:21:57.149
I think someone
wants to kill you.

163
00:22:03.333 --> 00:22:05.333
That wasn't very nice.

164
00:22:08.372 --> 00:22:10.544
- You were supposed
to shoot her.

165
00:22:10.549 --> 00:22:12.549
Well, I missed.

166
00:22:22.219 --> 00:22:24.219
Get Bond.

167
00:22:24.888 --> 00:22:26.039
- Where is he now?

168
00:22:26.044 --> 00:22:28.221
Approaching the
docks, Kings Quay.

169
00:22:31.528 --> 00:22:33.292
- Connecting.
- Tanner.

170
00:22:33.297 --> 00:22:34.426
I've got Bond.

171
00:22:34.431 --> 00:22:35.627
Ask him about Slate.

172
00:22:35.632 --> 00:22:37.362
She wants to know about Slate.

173
00:22:37.367 --> 00:22:39.031
Tell her Slate was a dead end.

174
00:22:39.036 --> 00:22:40.199
Slate was a dead end.

175
00:22:40.204 --> 00:22:41.533
Connection terminated.

176
00:22:41.538 --> 00:22:43.538
Damn him. He killed him.

177
00:23:16.339 --> 00:23:18.339
Touch me and I'll
break your wrist.

178
00:23:29.619 --> 00:23:31.619
Camille.

179
00:23:31.921 --> 00:23:33.921
How nice to see you.

180
00:23:34.357 --> 00:23:36.357
Alive, you mean?

181
00:23:37.293 --> 00:23:40.319
I knew we shouldn't
have slept together.

182
00:23:40.429 --> 00:23:42.829
I think I'm starting
to like you.

183
00:23:42.932 --> 00:23:45.696
So you did just try
and have me killed.

184
00:23:46.636 --> 00:23:48.339
And that made me very sad...

185
00:23:48.344 --> 00:23:50.595
thinking I would
never see you again.

186
00:23:51.541 --> 00:23:53.371
But here you are.

187
00:23:53.376 --> 00:23:56.209
Damn it, Dominic.
I was trying to help you.

188
00:23:59.715 --> 00:24:02.149
I was trying to
uncover a leak.

189
00:24:02.218 --> 00:24:04.379
And you, you sent
someone to kill me?

190
00:24:04.487 --> 00:24:07.354
Please don't talk to
me like I'm stupid.

191
00:24:08.991 --> 00:24:10.991
It's unattractive.

192
00:24:13.062 --> 00:24:15.724
Come. I wanna show
you something.

193
00:24:17.833 --> 00:24:19.564
Come.

194
00:24:19.569 --> 00:24:21.832
There's nothing that makes me
more uncomfortable...

195
00:24:21.837 --> 00:24:24.237
than friends talking
behind my back.

196
00:24:24.340 --> 00:24:26.340
It feels like...

197
00:24:26.842 --> 00:24:28.842
ants under my skin.

198
00:24:29.745 --> 00:24:32.213
It's been that way forever.

199
00:24:32.315 --> 00:24:34.340
I remember when I was 15.

200
00:24:34.984 --> 00:24:36.233
I had a crush on...

201
00:24:36.238 --> 00:24:38.476
one of my mother's
piano students.

202
00:24:39.188 --> 00:24:43.852
Somehow I overheard her saying
very nasty things about me.

203
00:24:45.094 --> 00:24:47.094
I got so angry.

204
00:24:48.097 --> 00:24:50.097
I took an iron.

205
00:24:53.235 --> 00:24:55.235
Is that him?

206
00:24:55.538 --> 00:24:58.006
I... We only spoke
on the phone.

207
00:25:00.610 --> 00:25:01.838
It's such a shame...

208
00:25:01.843 --> 00:25:04.239
because he's one of
my best geologists.

209
00:25:04.780 --> 00:25:07.681
He said you asked
to buy information.

210
00:25:08.784 --> 00:25:09.942
No. He called me...

211
00:25:09.947 --> 00:25:12.083
and offered to sell
me information.

212
00:25:14.190 --> 00:25:17.091
Why would I come back here
if I was lying?

213
00:25:17.927 --> 00:25:19.423
Because you love me.

214
00:25:19.428 --> 00:25:21.555
I was doing it for you.

215
00:25:21.631 --> 00:25:24.065
To stop him from
betraying you.

216
00:25:25.768 --> 00:25:29.204
You know what burns more
than all your bullshit?

217
00:25:30.039 --> 00:25:31.715
Is that I always
got the feeling...

218
00:25:31.720 --> 00:25:33.571
that you were only
sleeping with me...

219
00:25:33.576 --> 00:25:35.737
to get to General Medrano.

220
00:25:37.813 --> 00:25:39.813
Is that him?

221
00:25:40.249 --> 00:25:43.309
You know how these
deposed dictators are,

222
00:25:43.419 --> 00:25:45.444
jealous of their safety.

223
00:25:47.423 --> 00:25:49.423
Stick around.

224
00:25:49.759 --> 00:25:51.759
I'll introduce you.

225
00:25:53.596 --> 00:25:55.292
Do you see the girl
that just walked in here?

226
00:25:55.297 --> 00:25:58.391
Could you give her that?
Tell her to call me.

227
00:26:16.652 --> 00:26:18.880
You've reached
Universal Exports.

228
00:26:18.885 --> 00:26:21.112
Our offices are
currently closed.

229
00:26:28.864 --> 00:26:31.264
And you can do
all this for me?

230
00:26:32.268 --> 00:26:35.260
Well, look at what we
did to this country.

231
00:26:35.337 --> 00:26:36.834
The Haitians elect a priest...

232
00:26:36.839 --> 00:26:39.643
who decides to raise
the minimum wage...

233
00:26:39.648 --> 00:26:41.648
from 38 cents to $1 a day.

234
00:26:41.711 --> 00:26:42.582
It's not a lot,

235
00:26:42.587 --> 00:26:45.147
but it's enough to upset
the corporations...

236
00:26:45.214 --> 00:26:48.672
who were here making T-shirts
and running shoes.

237
00:26:48.784 --> 00:26:52.845
So they called us,
and we facilitated a change.

238
00:26:52.955 --> 00:26:54.117
The difference is,

239
00:26:54.122 --> 00:26:56.267
my country's not
some flyspeck...

240
00:26:56.272 --> 00:26:58.286
in the middle of
the Caribbean.

241
00:26:58.359 --> 00:27:01.795
But we've already begun
destabilizing the government.

242
00:27:01.863 --> 00:27:04.297
We'll supply the
private security.

243
00:27:04.365 --> 00:27:06.526
We'll pay off the
right officials,

244
00:27:06.634 --> 00:27:08.433
and we have 26 countries...

245
00:27:08.438 --> 00:27:10.570
ready to officially
recognize...

246
00:27:10.672 --> 00:27:13.140
your new Bolivian government.

247
00:27:14.142 --> 00:27:16.372
You want your country back.

248
00:27:16.745 --> 00:27:19.069
My organization can
give it to you...

249
00:27:19.074 --> 00:27:21.074
within the week.

250
00:27:22.150 --> 00:27:24.150
You've been busy.

251
00:27:24.185 --> 00:27:26.653
And in return you want what?

252
00:27:27.822 --> 00:27:29.822
A desert.

253
00:27:36.331 --> 00:27:38.891
- This part.
- This land is worthless.

254
00:27:40.869 --> 00:27:42.894
So you're getting
a great deal.

255
00:27:43.004 --> 00:27:45.004
You won't find oil there.

256
00:27:45.039 --> 00:27:47.064
Everyone has tried.

257
00:27:47.175 --> 00:27:49.507
Maybe, maybe not.

258
00:27:50.445 --> 00:27:53.346
But we own whatever we find.

259
00:28:00.855 --> 00:28:03.722
Did you know Ernesto Montes?

260
00:28:03.792 --> 00:28:06.226
A very powerful
man in his day.

261
00:28:06.294 --> 00:28:08.762
He had a beautiful
Russian wife.

262
00:28:09.697 --> 00:28:11.697
A dancer.

263
00:28:11.866 --> 00:28:14.300
Well, his daughter
works for me.

264
00:28:14.903 --> 00:28:16.866
Or did.

265
00:28:16.871 --> 00:28:18.871
She's lovely,

266
00:28:18.907 --> 00:28:21.034
but I don't see
the resemblance.

267
00:28:21.109 --> 00:28:22.884
Why don't you consider her...

268
00:28:22.889 --> 00:28:24.909
as something to
sweeten the deal?

269
00:28:27.816 --> 00:28:29.749
Just promise me to drop her...

270
00:28:29.754 --> 00:28:31.754
over the side
when you're done.

271
00:28:33.388 --> 00:28:36.050
Camille, General Medrano.

272
00:28:51.906 --> 00:28:54.670
Be careful what you
wish for, my dear.

273
00:29:03.918 --> 00:29:05.918
Have fun, you two.

274
00:30:24.365 --> 00:30:25.495
What the hell are you doing?

275
00:30:25.500 --> 00:30:27.597
- You're welcome.
- You idiot. Take me back.

276
00:30:27.602 --> 00:30:30.196
You know, maybe
I'll do that later.

277
00:30:33.708 --> 00:30:35.869
You're not one of Greene's.

278
00:30:37.045 --> 00:30:39.045
Dominic Greene?

279
00:30:42.183 --> 00:30:44.183
Get down.

280
00:31:08.375 --> 00:31:10.605
- Give me the wheel.
- Navigate.

281
00:31:16.717 --> 00:31:18.717
Left.

282
00:31:28.829 --> 00:31:31.059
- What are you doing?
- Hold on.

283
00:31:47.914 --> 00:31:49.914
Get down.

284
00:33:09.029 --> 00:33:10.592
Excuse me.

285
00:33:10.597 --> 00:33:12.758
Thank you. She's seasick.

286
00:33:45.365 --> 00:33:46.895
It's Bond.

287
00:33:46.900 --> 00:33:48.959
- Connect Bond.
- Connecting 007.

288
00:33:49.069 --> 00:33:50.198
Yes?

289
00:33:50.203 --> 00:33:52.364
Name check, Dominic Greene.

290
00:33:52.439 --> 00:33:54.439
G- R-E-E-N-E.

291
00:33:56.877 --> 00:33:57.973
I might need a little
more than that.

292
00:33:57.978 --> 00:33:59.107
There are a lot of
Dominic Greenes.

293
00:33:59.112 --> 00:34:01.209
Do you have a social security
or passport number?

294
00:34:01.214 --> 00:34:02.577
No.

295
00:34:02.582 --> 00:34:03.979
Scanning DGSE databases.

296
00:34:03.984 --> 00:34:06.953
- Anything?
- Scanning KGB databases.

297
00:34:07.053 --> 00:34:09.317
Do you have anything?
Will you put her on, please?

298
00:34:09.322 --> 00:34:11.916
I am on, Bond. What
happened to Slate?

299
00:34:11.992 --> 00:34:13.288
I'm not dwelling on the past.

300
00:34:13.293 --> 00:34:14.828
- I don't think
you should, either.

301
00:34:14.833 --> 00:34:15.490
You killed him.

302
00:34:15.495 --> 00:34:18.487
Largest hit, Dominic Greene,
CEO of Greene Planet.

303
00:34:18.598 --> 00:34:20.529
It's a utility company,

304
00:34:20.534 --> 00:34:23.084
but Greene's been doing
a lot of philanthropic work,

305
00:34:23.103 --> 00:34:25.853
buying up large tracts of land
for ecological preserves.

306
00:34:25.939 --> 00:34:28.931
You should be getting
his picture now.

307
00:34:29.009 --> 00:34:31.009
Yep, that's him.

308
00:34:31.178 --> 00:34:32.256
I'm afraid there's
a firewall...

309
00:34:32.261 --> 00:34:33.475
around his other
corporate holdings,

310
00:34:33.480 --> 00:34:34.776
so we have no
other information.

311
00:34:34.781 --> 00:34:36.311
Get me the Americans.

312
00:34:36.316 --> 00:34:37.812
Connecting.

313
00:34:37.817 --> 00:34:38.947
Go ahead.

314
00:34:38.952 --> 00:34:41.614
Interest in Dominic Greene,
Greene Planet.

315
00:34:41.688 --> 00:34:43.688
Transferring you now.

316
00:34:45.358 --> 00:34:47.622
Hold for Gregory Beam, please.

317
00:34:48.528 --> 00:34:49.658
Thank you.

318
00:34:49.663 --> 00:34:51.663
Hi, this is Gregory
Beam, ma 'am.

319
00:34:51.665 --> 00:34:53.361
Hello, Mr. Beam.

320
00:34:53.366 --> 00:34:55.134
I'm so sorry to
keep you waiting.

321
00:34:55.139 --> 00:34:57.032
We have no interest
in Mr. Greene.

322
00:34:57.037 --> 00:34:58.533
Thank you, Mr. Beam.

323
00:34:58.538 --> 00:34:59.701
Connection terminated.

324
00:34:59.706 --> 00:35:01.536
He's a person of
extreme interest.

325
00:35:01.541 --> 00:35:02.861
- But he just said
that he wasn't...

326
00:35:02.866 --> 00:35:04.039
Tanner, I asked
about the man...

327
00:35:04.044 --> 00:35:05.112
and she transferred me...

328
00:35:05.117 --> 00:35:06.741
to the section chief
of South America.

329
00:35:06.746 --> 00:35:09.646
How would she know to do that
if they weren't tracking him?

330
00:35:14.320 --> 00:35:16.850
Bond, we have your location
as approaching an airfield.

331
00:35:16.855 --> 00:35:18.752
- Is Greene on the move?
- Yeah.

332
00:35:18.757 --> 00:35:20.082
I've got a tail number.

333
00:35:20.087 --> 00:35:22.056
Golf-Zero-Charli
e-Sierra-Charlie.

334
00:35:22.061 --> 00:35:24.061
Get me a destination.

335
00:35:26.832 --> 00:35:28.395
It's a private charter...

336
00:35:28.400 --> 00:35:31.494
going to Bregenz, Austria,
leaving immediately.

337
00:35:32.037 --> 00:35:34.665
Tanner, authorize
a charter for 007.

338
00:35:36.108 --> 00:35:38.214
And, Bond, if you
could avoid killing...

339
00:35:38.219 --> 00:35:39.373
every possible lead,

340
00:35:39.378 --> 00:35:41.108
it would be deeply
appreciated.

341
00:35:41.113 --> 00:35:43.343
Yes, ma'am. I'll do my best.

342
00:35:43.882 --> 00:35:45.579
Connection terminated.

343
00:35:45.584 --> 00:35:47.584
I've heard that before.

344
00:35:49.888 --> 00:35:51.685
- Hello.
- Hi.

345
00:35:51.690 --> 00:35:53.690
Welcome aboard.

346
00:35:56.528 --> 00:35:58.528
Come. Have a seat.

347
00:35:59.031 --> 00:36:01.124
Charlie-Sierra-Charlie.

348
00:36:16.382 --> 00:36:18.045
Jeez.

349
00:36:18.050 --> 00:36:20.050
Sorry.

350
00:36:23.055 --> 00:36:25.055
How much longer?

351
00:36:27.092 --> 00:36:29.151
So do we have an
understanding?

352
00:36:30.262 --> 00:36:31.392
Yeah.

353
00:36:31.397 --> 00:36:33.130
We do nothing to stop
a coup in Bolivia,

354
00:36:33.135 --> 00:36:33.827
and in exchange,

355
00:36:33.832 --> 00:36:36.366
the new government
gives America...

356
00:36:36.371 --> 00:36:38.371
the lease to any oil found.

357
00:36:39.772 --> 00:36:41.772
If it's oil you want.

358
00:36:42.808 --> 00:36:45.675
Well, you didn't find
diamonds, did you?

359
00:36:51.183 --> 00:36:52.949
Drilling underground,
you kept off...

360
00:36:52.954 --> 00:36:54.815
everybody's radar
for a very long time,

361
00:36:54.820 --> 00:36:57.018
but you can't buy
that much piping...

362
00:36:57.023 --> 00:36:59.023
without somebody
getting curious.

363
00:37:00.092 --> 00:37:02.092
We'll have to verify the find.

364
00:37:02.161 --> 00:37:04.579
I'm not even admitting
there is one.

365
00:37:04.584 --> 00:37:06.598
You are getting this for free.

366
00:37:07.599 --> 00:37:10.432
Venezuela, Brazil,
now Bolivia.

367
00:37:10.502 --> 00:37:12.738
With you tied up in
the Middle East.

368
00:37:12.743 --> 00:37:15.166
South America is
falling like dominoes.

369
00:37:16.608 --> 00:37:18.993
You don't need another
Marxist giving...

370
00:37:18.998 --> 00:37:21.443
national resources to
the people, do you?

371
00:37:22.114 --> 00:37:23.208
Well, we can hardly
be expected...

372
00:37:23.213 --> 00:37:24.211
to do something
about a coup...

373
00:37:24.216 --> 00:37:26.216
we know nothing about.

374
00:37:29.621 --> 00:37:31.782
And I have a pest.

375
00:37:33.459 --> 00:37:35.459
This.

376
00:37:37.830 --> 00:37:40.298
You have any idea who that is?

377
00:37:50.376 --> 00:37:52.376
Sorry.

378
00:37:54.146 --> 00:37:56.876
It's James Bond,
British Secret Service.

379
00:37:57.850 --> 00:38:00.751
I don't know how I
could have missed that.

380
00:38:02.321 --> 00:38:05.085
I will need you to
get rid of him for me.

381
00:38:05.190 --> 00:38:07.818
Yeah. That's not
gonna be a problem.

382
00:38:24.610 --> 00:38:25.520
You know who Greene is...

383
00:38:25.525 --> 00:38:26.874
and you wanna put
us in bed with him.

384
00:38:26.879 --> 00:38:28.879
You are kidding, right?

385
00:38:28.914 --> 00:38:30.042
Yeah. You're right.

386
00:38:30.047 --> 00:38:32.247
We should just deal
with nice people.

387
00:38:32.351 --> 00:38:35.047
I need to know you're
on the team, Felix.

388
00:38:35.120 --> 00:38:37.714
I need to know you
value your career.

389
00:39:50.328 --> 00:39:52.328
Dominic Greene.

390
00:40:10.681 --> 00:40:12.545
- Good to see you. Good.
- How are you?

391
00:40:12.550 --> 00:40:14.550
Thank you.

392
00:40:48.886 --> 00:40:50.911
Ladies and gentlemen,

393
00:40:51.022 --> 00:40:54.480
tonight's performance of Tosca
will begin shortly.

394
00:40:54.559 --> 00:40:56.559
Please take your seats.

395
00:41:51.148 --> 00:41:53.912
What else does General
Medrano require?

396
00:42:16.073 --> 00:42:18.507
Anything further
from Canadian intelligence?

397
00:42:18.609 --> 00:42:20.668
We'll discuss that later.

398
00:42:21.178 --> 00:42:23.544
How much more
pipeline do we need?

399
00:42:23.648 --> 00:42:26.173
Ideally, 2,000 kilometers.

400
00:42:26.651 --> 00:42:28.710
Are there any objections?

401
00:42:29.854 --> 00:42:30.983
No.

402
00:42:30.988 --> 00:42:32.385
Not here.

403
00:42:32.390 --> 00:42:34.390
No objections.

404
00:42:34.458 --> 00:42:37.621
Transfer the funds
from our Siberian holdings.

405
00:42:37.695 --> 00:42:39.695
Done.

406
00:42:42.533 --> 00:42:44.533
Where do the Americans stand?

407
00:42:44.635 --> 00:42:46.924
Well, the CIA doesn't
care about another...

408
00:42:46.929 --> 00:42:49.004
dictator as long as
they get their end.

409
00:42:49.073 --> 00:42:51.633
But when they find out
that they've been duped?

410
00:42:51.709 --> 00:42:53.709
I'm working on that.

411
00:42:53.744 --> 00:42:55.841
I'm still not sure that
the Tierra Project...

412
00:42:55.846 --> 00:42:57.476
is the best use of
Quantum 's time.

413
00:42:57.481 --> 00:42:59.912
Perhaps we should shift
our focus to the Canadian.

414
00:42:59.917 --> 00:43:02.647
This is the world's
most precious resource.

415
00:43:02.720 --> 00:43:05.985
We need to control as much
of it as we can.

416
00:43:06.057 --> 00:43:08.321
Bolivia must be top priority.

417
00:43:08.392 --> 00:43:10.392
Can I offer an opinion?

418
00:43:12.663 --> 00:43:14.395
I really think you people...

419
00:43:14.400 --> 00:43:16.565
should find a better
place to meet.

420
00:43:22.206 --> 00:43:24.766
Where do you think
you're going?

421
00:43:45.428 --> 00:43:47.428
Thank you.

422
00:43:56.940 --> 00:43:59.374
Well, Tosca isn't
for everyone.

423
00:45:13.349 --> 00:45:15.349
Drop it.

424
00:45:18.321 --> 00:45:20.619
So who are you working for?

425
00:45:20.690 --> 00:45:22.287
Piss off.

426
00:45:22.292 --> 00:45:24.823
Get rid of anything
we brought with us.

427
00:45:24.828 --> 00:45:26.828
We've been compromised.

428
00:45:29.332 --> 00:45:32.028
I asked you who you
were working for.

429
00:45:43.980 --> 00:45:46.380
- Is he one of ours?
- No.

430
00:45:46.482 --> 00:45:49.042
Then he shouldn't
be looking at me.

431
00:45:57.694 --> 00:45:59.694
Get me M.

432
00:46:00.663 --> 00:46:02.060
It's your line.

433
00:46:02.065 --> 00:46:04.499
Thanks. Connect call.

434
00:46:04.567 --> 00:46:06.097
Connecting Tanner.

435
00:46:06.102 --> 00:46:07.665
We've ID'd the pictures.

436
00:46:07.670 --> 00:46:09.033
Show me.

437
00:46:09.038 --> 00:46:11.168
Gregor Karakov,
former minister,

438
00:46:11.173 --> 00:46:13.702
now owns most of the
mines in Siberia.

439
00:46:13.776 --> 00:46:17.439
Moishe Soref, former Mossad,
now telecom giant,

440
00:46:17.547 --> 00:46:20.345
and Guy Haines, special envoy
to the Prime Minister.

441
00:46:20.416 --> 00:46:21.746
Get Bond.

442
00:46:21.751 --> 00:46:23.581
There's something else.

443
00:46:23.586 --> 00:46:25.507
It appears Bond
shot Haines'...

444
00:46:25.512 --> 00:46:27.682
bodyguard and threw
him off a roof.

445
00:46:31.728 --> 00:46:33.591
- Where are you?
- Did you get my pictures?

446
00:46:33.596 --> 00:46:35.960
Was this a conversation?
Can you link these people?

447
00:46:35.965 --> 00:46:37.428
Is that stress in your voice?

448
00:46:37.433 --> 00:46:39.063
I need you to come
in and debrief.

449
00:46:39.068 --> 00:46:40.237
- I don't have time.

450
00:46:40.242 --> 00:46:42.242
Bond, you killed
a man in Bregenz.

451
00:46:42.305 --> 00:46:43.601
I did my best not to.

452
00:46:43.606 --> 00:46:45.570
You shot him at point blank
and threw him off a roof.

453
00:46:45.575 --> 00:46:47.575
I'd hardly call that
showing restraint,

454
00:46:47.610 --> 00:46:50.110
especially since he was
a member of Special Branch.

455
00:46:53.583 --> 00:46:54.812
So who was he guarding?

456
00:46:54.817 --> 00:46:55.947
Bond, are you
missing the fact...

457
00:46:55.952 --> 00:46:57.548
that you killed a member
of Special Branch?

458
00:46:57.553 --> 00:46:59.553
I need you to come in.

459
00:46:59.589 --> 00:47:02.042
And I would, but right
now I need to find...

460
00:47:02.047 --> 00:47:03.788
the man who tried to kill you.

461
00:47:03.793 --> 00:47:05.056
Go back to sleep.

462
00:47:05.061 --> 00:47:06.424
Connection terminated.

463
00:47:06.429 --> 00:47:07.926
Restrict Bond's movements.

464
00:47:07.931 --> 00:47:09.627
Cancel his cards.

465
00:47:09.632 --> 00:47:11.462
Put an alert on his passports.
All of them.

466
00:47:11.467 --> 00:47:13.798
And I want to know everything
we don't know about Haines.

467
00:47:13.803 --> 00:47:14.933
Yes, ma 'am.

468
00:47:14.938 --> 00:47:15.734
And, Tanner,

469
00:47:15.739 --> 00:47:18.066
be careful who you
trust with this.

470
00:47:18.141 --> 00:47:19.798
Hopefully, you're
a better judge...

471
00:47:19.803 --> 00:47:21.803
of character than I am.

472
00:47:22.111 --> 00:47:23.712
You want to follow
your friends...

473
00:47:23.717 --> 00:47:24.642
to La Paz, Bolivia?

474
00:47:24.647 --> 00:47:26.647
Please.

475
00:47:28.318 --> 00:47:29.981
I'm sorry, sir, but
this doesn't work.

476
00:47:29.986 --> 00:47:32.318
Do you have another card?

477
00:47:32.422 --> 00:47:34.422
No.

478
00:47:38.994 --> 00:47:40.994
Could you do me a favor?

479
00:47:41.096 --> 00:47:42.993
You're gonna get a
phone call in a minute.

480
00:47:42.998 --> 00:47:46.434
Would you mind telling them
I'm headed for Cairo?

481
00:47:46.501 --> 00:47:48.867
- I'd be happy to.
- Thank you.

482
00:48:28.877 --> 00:48:30.877
Mathis.

483
00:48:31.013 --> 00:48:32.976
What do you want?

484
00:48:32.981 --> 00:48:34.981
Come to apologize?

485
00:48:37.052 --> 00:48:39.052
You know, Mathis.

486
00:48:39.354 --> 00:48:41.584
I think retirement suits you.

487
00:48:42.357 --> 00:48:44.357
None for him.

488
00:48:44.493 --> 00:48:46.757
Sorry. He's in a
bad mood today.

489
00:49:10.285 --> 00:49:12.515
I need a passport
and matching credit cards.

490
00:49:13.422 --> 00:49:15.617
And Ml6 ran out of plastic?

491
00:49:17.025 --> 00:49:17.974
Well, oddly, right now,

492
00:49:17.979 --> 00:49:19.756
you're the only person
I think I can trust.

493
00:49:19.761 --> 00:49:21.558
That is odd.

494
00:49:21.563 --> 00:49:23.460
But I guess when one's young,

495
00:49:23.465 --> 00:49:25.701
it seems very easy
to distinguish...

496
00:49:25.706 --> 00:49:27.264
between right and wrong.

497
00:49:27.269 --> 00:49:30.238
But as one gets older,
it becomes more difficult.

498
00:49:30.305 --> 00:49:33.297
The villains and the heroes
get all mixed up.

499
00:49:34.276 --> 00:49:36.710
I was sorry to
hear about Vesper.

500
00:49:37.212 --> 00:49:39.212
I think she loved you.

501
00:49:40.215 --> 00:49:42.547
Right up until the moment
she betrayed me.

502
00:49:43.452 --> 00:49:45.452
She died for you.

503
00:49:47.222 --> 00:49:49.588
Why did you really
want to see me?

504
00:49:51.226 --> 00:49:53.226
I need some information.

505
00:49:57.299 --> 00:49:59.096
You have some hard friends.

506
00:49:59.101 --> 00:50:01.565
This man is some
kind of facilitator.

507
00:50:01.636 --> 00:50:02.968
Fingers in many pies,

508
00:50:02.973 --> 00:50:05.003
and they don't
leave any prints.

509
00:50:05.107 --> 00:50:06.760
- These men were together?

510
00:50:06.765 --> 00:50:08.765
They're buying
up oil pipeline.

511
00:50:08.810 --> 00:50:10.407
Something called
the Tierra Project.

512
00:50:10.412 --> 00:50:12.778
- Do you know it?
- Destroy these.

513
00:50:12.848 --> 00:50:15.248
That's Guy Haines.
You don't know him?

514
00:50:15.317 --> 00:50:17.317
- Should I?
- I suppose not.

515
00:50:17.319 --> 00:50:20.379
You haven't been keeping
secrets as long as I have.

516
00:50:20.489 --> 00:50:22.489
He keeps a very low profile,

517
00:50:22.524 --> 00:50:25.073
but he's one of the
Prime Minister's...

518
00:50:25.078 --> 00:50:26.289
closest advisors.

519
00:50:26.294 --> 00:50:28.044
Well, they say
you're judged...

520
00:50:28.049 --> 00:50:29.960
by the strength
of your enemies.

521
00:50:29.965 --> 00:50:32.058
Do you know anything
about Bolivia?

522
00:50:32.167 --> 00:50:34.359
I was stationed in
South America...

523
00:50:34.364 --> 00:50:35.465
for seven years.

524
00:50:35.470 --> 00:50:37.931
- Well, do you have
some contacts there?

525
00:50:37.936 --> 00:50:38.735
A few.

526
00:50:38.740 --> 00:50:40.867
What do you want to know?

527
00:50:41.743 --> 00:50:43.743
Come with me.

528
00:51:13.942 --> 00:51:15.942
You can't sleep?

529
00:51:16.278 --> 00:51:18.208
May I fix you a drink, sir?

530
00:51:18.213 --> 00:51:20.213
What are you drinking?

531
00:51:20.882 --> 00:51:22.907
I don't know. What
am I drinking?

532
00:51:23.018 --> 00:51:24.952
Three measures
of Gordon's gin,

533
00:51:24.957 --> 00:51:26.550
one of vodka, half of...

534
00:51:26.555 --> 00:51:27.417
- Kina Lillet.

535
00:51:27.422 --> 00:51:29.581
Kina Lillet, which
is not Vermouth,

536
00:51:29.691 --> 00:51:31.454
shaken well until
it is ice-cold,

537
00:51:31.459 --> 00:51:32.345
then served...

538
00:51:32.350 --> 00:51:34.758
with a large thin
slice of lemon peel.

539
00:51:35.297 --> 00:51:37.127
Six of them.

540
00:51:37.132 --> 00:51:38.895
That's impressive.

541
00:51:38.900 --> 00:51:41.299
They're good. You
should have one.

542
00:51:41.402 --> 00:51:43.893
No, it'll just keep me awake.

543
00:51:48.309 --> 00:51:50.641
So what's keeping you awake?

544
00:51:53.380 --> 00:51:56.042
I was wondering why
you came with me.

545
00:51:57.651 --> 00:52:00.882
It takes something
to admit you were wrong.

546
00:52:03.891 --> 00:52:06.257
- You want a sleeping pill?
- No.

547
00:52:06.327 --> 00:52:08.057
- Pain pill?
- No.

548
00:52:08.062 --> 00:52:10.155
I have pills for everything.

549
00:52:10.664 --> 00:52:12.664
Some make you taller.

550
00:52:13.734 --> 00:52:15.734
Some make you forget.

551
00:52:18.906 --> 00:52:21.340
I'm going to try
and get some sleep.

552
00:52:21.442 --> 00:52:23.442
Good idea.

553
00:52:37.758 --> 00:52:39.622
Thank you.

554
00:52:39.627 --> 00:52:42.619
Mr. Bond, my name is Fields.
I'm from the consulate.

555
00:52:42.696 --> 00:52:43.826
Well, of course you are.

556
00:52:43.831 --> 00:52:45.194
And what do you do
at the consulate, Fields?

557
00:52:45.199 --> 00:52:46.595
That's not important.

558
00:52:46.600 --> 00:52:47.930
My orders are to
turn you around...

559
00:52:47.935 --> 00:52:50.032
and put you on the first plane
back to London.

560
00:52:50.037 --> 00:52:52.801
Do those orders include
my friend Mathis?

561
00:52:52.873 --> 00:52:54.670
I'm sorry, I don't
know who you are.

562
00:52:54.675 --> 00:52:56.695
You see that? Gone
such a short time...

563
00:52:56.700 --> 00:52:57.940
and already forgotten.

564
00:52:57.945 --> 00:52:59.708
You're just saying
that to hurt me.

565
00:52:59.713 --> 00:53:01.381
Mr. Bond, these
orders come from...

566
00:53:01.386 --> 00:53:02.945
the highest
possible authority.

567
00:53:02.950 --> 00:53:03.260
Taxi.

568
00:53:03.265 --> 00:53:05.885
Fields, when is the
next flight to London?

569
00:53:05.986 --> 00:53:07.483
Tomorrow morning.

570
00:53:07.488 --> 00:53:08.617
Well then, we have all night.

571
00:53:08.622 --> 00:53:10.219
If you attempt to flee,
I will arrest you,

572
00:53:10.224 --> 00:53:11.221
drop you off in jail...

573
00:53:11.226 --> 00:53:12.788
and take you to the
plane in chains.

574
00:53:12.793 --> 00:53:15.284
- Understand?
- Perfectly. After you.

575
00:53:17.298 --> 00:53:20.131
- I think she has handcuffs.
- I do hope so.

576
00:53:28.909 --> 00:53:31.209
He blames the water shortage
on global warming.

577
00:53:32.046 --> 00:53:34.046
Hello, Carlos? Carlos.

578
00:53:37.918 --> 00:53:39.968
The Colonel who heads
the National Police.

579
00:54:04.845 --> 00:54:06.845
We have a reservation.

580
00:54:07.681 --> 00:54:09.244
- Cَmo estل?
- Very well, thank you.

581
00:54:09.249 --> 00:54:11.615
- Your name?
- Miss Fields.

582
00:54:16.357 --> 00:54:18.357
- You're going nowhere.
- So shoot me.

583
00:54:18.359 --> 00:54:19.455
I'd rather stay in a morgue.

584
00:54:19.460 --> 00:54:22.691
We are teachers on sabbatical.
This fits our cover.

585
00:54:22.763 --> 00:54:25.527
No, it doesn't.
Get in. Get in.

586
00:54:51.925 --> 00:54:53.925
Follow me, please.

587
00:55:01.235 --> 00:55:02.990
- May I show you
your room, seٌor?

588
00:55:02.995 --> 00:55:04.995
No, it's fine. Thank you.

589
00:55:21.755 --> 00:55:23.916
I can't find the...

590
00:55:24.691 --> 00:55:26.691
The stationery.

591
00:55:27.194 --> 00:55:29.389
Will you come
and help me look?

592
00:55:43.644 --> 00:55:45.839
You've been
invited to a party.

593
00:55:45.946 --> 00:55:48.540
I didn't know we had
any friends here.

594
00:55:49.615 --> 00:55:51.615
Greene Planet.

595
00:55:52.318 --> 00:55:53.448
You're not coming?

596
00:55:53.453 --> 00:55:55.683
I'm having a drink
with my friend the Colonel.

597
00:55:55.688 --> 00:55:58.020
I'll see you there later.

598
00:56:02.962 --> 00:56:05.658
Do you know how
angry I am at myself?

599
00:56:06.165 --> 00:56:08.165
I can't imagine.

600
00:56:10.670 --> 00:56:12.670
You must be furious.

601
00:56:19.145 --> 00:56:21.375
Do you want to go to a party?

602
00:56:22.014 --> 00:56:24.014
A party?

603
00:56:24.083 --> 00:56:26.210
But I have nothing to wear.

604
00:56:26.652 --> 00:56:28.652
We'll fix that.

605
00:56:47.340 --> 00:56:49.672
It might be useful to
know your real name.

606
00:56:49.742 --> 00:56:51.742
Fields.

607
00:56:53.779 --> 00:56:55.779
Just Fields.

608
00:56:56.282 --> 00:56:58.012
Fields it is, then.

609
00:56:58.017 --> 00:57:01.783
We are in a spiral
of environmental decline.

610
00:57:02.889 --> 00:57:09.021
Since 1945, 17% of the
planet's vegetated surface...

611
00:57:09.095 --> 00:57:11.962
has been irreversibly
degraded.

612
00:57:12.732 --> 00:57:15.739
The Tierra Project is
just one small part...

613
00:57:15.744 --> 00:57:18.136
of a global network
of Eco Parks...

614
00:57:18.237 --> 00:57:20.262
that Greene Planet
has created...

615
00:57:20.373 --> 00:57:24.776
to rejuvenate a world
on the verge of collapse.

616
00:57:26.546 --> 00:57:28.592
I hope that
tonight you make...

617
00:57:28.597 --> 00:57:30.710
the decision to
be part of that.

618
00:57:32.752 --> 00:57:34.752
Thank you.

619
00:57:38.391 --> 00:57:40.391
And have fun.

620
00:57:40.426 --> 00:57:42.621
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

621
00:57:43.396 --> 00:57:45.421
Excellent speech
and congratulations.

622
00:57:45.498 --> 00:57:47.625
Wonderful speech, Dominic.

623
00:57:47.733 --> 00:57:49.733
- We need you here.
- Thank you.

624
00:57:49.735 --> 00:57:53.000
Miss Fields, Mr. Bond,
my friend Carlos.

625
00:57:53.105 --> 00:57:55.105
- Pleased to meet you.
- Ma'am.

626
00:57:56.008 --> 00:57:59.000
Mr. Bond, Mathis has spoken
a great deal about you.

627
00:57:59.111 --> 00:58:00.982
I want you to
know my entire...

628
00:58:00.987 --> 00:58:02.987
police force is
at your disposal.

629
00:58:03.349 --> 00:58:04.845
Well, that could
be very useful.

630
00:58:04.850 --> 00:58:06.470
You know, there are
people in this...

631
00:58:06.475 --> 00:58:08.182
country spending half
their paycheck...

632
00:58:08.187 --> 00:58:09.784
just to get clean water.

633
00:58:09.789 --> 00:58:10.918
What do you think of that?

634
00:58:10.923 --> 00:58:12.982
The Bolivian government
is the problem.

635
00:58:13.092 --> 00:58:14.789
They cut down the trees,

636
00:58:14.794 --> 00:58:17.098
then act surprised
when the water...

637
00:58:17.103 --> 00:58:19.026
and the soil wash out to sea.

638
00:58:19.031 --> 00:58:20.331
I couldn't agree more.

639
00:58:20.336 --> 00:58:22.523
I hope this figure
is to your liking.

640
00:58:22.635 --> 00:58:25.001
Chéri, you shouldn't tease.

641
00:58:25.104 --> 00:58:27.061
Why don't you tell
them about all...

642
00:58:27.066 --> 00:58:29.131
the land you bought
up outside Potosي?

643
00:58:29.208 --> 00:58:31.438
It's been a pleasure.
Will you excuse me?

644
00:58:31.510 --> 00:58:32.940
Of course.

645
00:58:32.945 --> 00:58:34.141
Somehow the logging rights...

646
00:58:34.146 --> 00:58:36.596
went to a multinational
corporation...

647
00:58:36.601 --> 00:58:38.346
that cut down the forests,

648
00:58:38.351 --> 00:58:40.905
but only after our
last government...

649
00:58:40.910 --> 00:58:43.050
sold the land to
Greene Planet.

650
00:58:44.991 --> 00:58:47.067
- Or have I got
my facts crossed?

651
00:58:47.072 --> 00:58:49.072
Yes, I think you did.

652
00:58:49.161 --> 00:58:51.161
You'll excuse us?

653
00:58:51.831 --> 00:58:53.831
What a wonderful night.

654
00:58:57.069 --> 00:58:59.697
You just cost me
quite a bit of money, darling.

655
00:58:59.805 --> 00:59:02.467
You can't put a
price on integrity.

656
00:59:02.575 --> 00:59:04.575
I can try.

657
00:59:09.649 --> 00:59:11.045
Thank you.

658
00:59:11.050 --> 00:59:13.373
Tell me you didn't
drop by tonight...

659
00:59:13.378 --> 00:59:15.116
just to piss on my parade.

660
00:59:15.121 --> 00:59:16.718
Or are you still after...

661
00:59:16.723 --> 00:59:19.023
this General's head
for your mantel?

662
00:59:19.125 --> 00:59:20.688
A little of both.

663
00:59:20.693 --> 00:59:22.289
Tell me where Medrano is...

664
00:59:22.294 --> 00:59:25.354
and maybe you won't lose
any more investors.

665
00:59:28.968 --> 00:59:31.025
You are really
breaking my heart,

666
00:59:31.030 --> 00:59:33.337
choosing an insect
like that over me.

667
00:59:34.874 --> 00:59:36.704
Are you going to
throw me over?

668
00:59:36.709 --> 00:59:39.974
No. You've been drinking,
so maybe you slipped.

669
00:59:40.813 --> 00:59:43.304
Just think how much
you'd miss me.

670
00:59:48.754 --> 00:59:50.351
Good evening.

671
00:59:50.356 --> 00:59:52.356
There you are.

672
00:59:53.759 --> 00:59:55.759
Would you excuse me?

673
00:59:55.828 --> 00:59:57.828
Mr. Bond.

674
00:59:58.163 --> 01:00:00.163
What a pleasure.

675
01:00:02.000 --> 01:00:03.056
Well, careful with this one.

676
01:00:03.061 --> 01:00:04.230
She won't go to
bed with you...

677
01:00:04.235 --> 01:00:06.931
unless you give her something
she really wants.

678
01:00:07.038 --> 01:00:07.657
It's a shame...

679
01:00:07.662 --> 01:00:09.235
because she's really
quite stunning...

680
01:00:09.240 --> 01:00:12.073
once you get her on her back.

681
01:00:12.177 --> 01:00:14.839
I wish I could say
the feeling was mutual.

682
01:00:14.913 --> 01:00:16.276
I'm sorry, Mr. Greene,
but we have to go.

683
01:00:16.281 --> 01:00:18.579
Please. My friends
call me Dominic.

684
01:00:18.683 --> 01:00:20.683
I'm sure they do.

685
01:00:21.352 --> 01:00:23.843
How much do you know
about Bond, Camille?

686
01:00:23.922 --> 01:00:26.186
Because he's rather
a tragic case.

687
01:00:26.257 --> 01:00:29.192
As Ml6 says, he's
difficult to control.

688
01:00:29.260 --> 01:00:31.654
Nice way of saying
that everything...

689
01:00:31.659 --> 01:00:33.924
he touches seems
to wither and die.

690
01:00:34.032 --> 01:00:35.295
Shall we?

691
01:00:35.300 --> 01:00:37.860
Doesn't bode well
for you, I'm afraid.

692
01:00:37.936 --> 01:00:40.029
You two do make
a charming couple, though.

693
01:00:40.105 --> 01:00:43.040
You're both... What's
the expression?

694
01:00:43.108 --> 01:00:45.108
Damaged goods.

695
01:00:48.146 --> 01:00:50.146
Oh, my gosh.

696
01:00:50.582 --> 01:00:52.582
I'm so sorry.

697
01:00:55.887 --> 01:00:57.117
Come on, lighten up.

698
01:00:57.122 --> 01:00:59.122
You're cramping my style.

699
01:01:00.091 --> 01:01:02.091
So it's British
intelligence now.

700
01:01:02.127 --> 01:01:03.790
What the hell do
you want from me?

701
01:01:03.795 --> 01:01:04.856
You're gonna show me

702
01:01:04.861 --> 01:01:06.626
Dominic Greene's
Tierra Project.

703
01:01:06.631 --> 01:01:08.656
- Are you up to it?
- Do I have a choice?

704
01:01:08.767 --> 01:01:10.630
Do you want one?

705
01:01:10.635 --> 01:01:13.502
There's something horribly
efficient about you.

706
01:01:13.605 --> 01:01:15.605
Is that a compliment?

707
01:01:28.753 --> 01:01:31.255
Well, what's the bet
that Dominic Greene...

708
01:01:31.260 --> 01:01:33.260
has friends in
the police force?

709
01:01:44.269 --> 01:01:46.269
Stay here.

710
01:02:06.691 --> 01:02:09.319
Now, why would you
want me to do that?

711
01:02:40.825 --> 01:02:42.825
Mathis?

712
01:02:44.028 --> 01:02:47.088
There's a hospital
on the other side of town.

713
01:02:47.198 --> 01:02:49.198
Please.

714
01:02:49.567 --> 01:02:51.567
Stay with me.

715
01:02:51.903 --> 01:02:53.903
Stay here, please.

716
01:02:54.539 --> 01:02:56.202
Please.

717
01:02:56.207 --> 01:02:58.207
Come here.

718
01:03:01.012 --> 01:03:03.012
It's okay.

719
01:03:04.349 --> 01:03:06.179
That's better.

720
01:03:06.184 --> 01:03:08.184
That doesn't hurt.

721
01:03:11.055 --> 01:03:13.182
Is Mathis your cover name?

722
01:03:14.225 --> 01:03:16.225
Yes.

723
01:03:17.562 --> 01:03:19.689
Not a very good one, is it?

724
01:03:25.370 --> 01:03:27.565
Do we forgive each other?

725
01:03:29.908 --> 01:03:32.376
I shouldn't have
left you alone.

726
01:03:33.945 --> 01:03:35.945
Vesper.

727
01:03:36.547 --> 01:03:38.708
She gave everything for you.

728
01:03:41.052 --> 01:03:43.052
Forgive her.

729
01:03:44.589 --> 01:03:46.589
Forgive yourself.

730
01:04:07.744 --> 01:04:10.235
Is that how you
treat your friends?

731
01:04:11.682 --> 01:04:13.682
He wouldn't care.

732
01:04:19.589 --> 01:04:21.589
Let's go.

733
01:04:35.205 --> 01:04:38.174
The Foreign Secretary's
asking to see you.

734
01:04:38.775 --> 01:04:40.205
What don't I know?

735
01:04:40.210 --> 01:04:43.202
René Mathis has been
shot dead in Bolivia.

736
01:04:43.714 --> 01:04:46.046
The police claim it was Bond.

737
01:05:20.350 --> 01:05:21.680
How much did you pay him?

738
01:05:21.685 --> 01:05:22.852
Well, he wanted you,

739
01:05:22.857 --> 01:05:25.018
but I left him the
car as collateral.

740
01:05:25.122 --> 01:05:28.023
He'll make much more
when he sells us out.

741
01:05:30.727 --> 01:05:32.290
Right.

742
01:05:32.295 --> 01:05:34.820
Let's see if this
thing'll fly.

743
01:05:49.880 --> 01:05:51.143
Here.

744
01:05:51.148 --> 01:05:52.943
All the information
I found said...

745
01:05:52.948 --> 01:05:54.713
there was nothing
of value there,

746
01:05:54.718 --> 01:05:57.881
but Greene's geologist
had proof that there was.

747
01:06:01.258 --> 01:06:02.643
My sources tell me...

748
01:06:02.648 --> 01:06:04.694
you're Bolivian
Secret Service,

749
01:06:05.729 --> 01:06:07.729
or used to be,

750
01:06:08.331 --> 01:06:10.054
and that you
infiltrated Greene's...

751
01:06:10.059 --> 01:06:12.059
organization by
having sex with him.

752
01:06:12.669 --> 01:06:15.661
- That offends you?
- No, not in the slightest.

753
01:06:16.073 --> 01:06:18.337
So what's your
interest in Greene?

754
01:06:18.408 --> 01:06:19.561
Amongst other things,

755
01:06:19.566 --> 01:06:21.540
he tried to kill
a friend of mine.

756
01:06:21.545 --> 01:06:23.442
- A woman?
- Yes.

757
01:06:23.447 --> 01:06:25.077
But it's not what you think.

758
01:06:25.082 --> 01:06:27.915
- Your mother?
- She likes to think so.

759
01:06:31.755 --> 01:06:33.780
What's that down there?

760
01:06:36.293 --> 01:06:38.090
That's a sinkhole.

761
01:06:38.095 --> 01:06:40.290
There are a few around here.

762
01:06:41.364 --> 01:06:44.629
Just for the record,
I wasn't with Greene for my...

763
01:07:19.803 --> 01:07:21.803
Damn it.

764
01:07:50.500 --> 01:07:52.500
I think we lost him.

765
01:08:01.711 --> 01:08:03.711
He's coming fast.

766
01:08:50.392 --> 01:08:52.417
He's right behind you.

767
01:09:34.270 --> 01:09:36.270
Here. Put that on.

768
01:10:21.250 --> 01:10:23.250
Come on.

769
01:10:43.706 --> 01:10:45.706
Camille.

770
01:11:04.293 --> 01:11:06.743
According to the Bolivians,
it was a routine stop,

771
01:11:06.795 --> 01:11:08.538
and when they discovered
Mathis' body.

772
01:11:08.543 --> 01:11:09.827
Bond disarmed and shot them.

773
01:11:09.832 --> 01:11:11.268
Of course, there
are no witnesses...

774
01:11:11.273 --> 01:11:12.029
to prove otherwise.

775
01:11:12.034 --> 01:11:14.832
I need something.
I can't go in there unarmed.

776
01:11:14.937 --> 01:11:17.030
I'm sorry. There's nothing.

777
01:11:19.441 --> 01:11:21.441
Come in.

778
01:11:22.211 --> 01:11:25.669
What's today's excuse?
That Bond is legally blind?

779
01:11:25.781 --> 01:11:27.010
No, Minister.

780
01:11:27.015 --> 01:11:28.793
I don't think I
need to tell you...

781
01:11:28.798 --> 01:11:30.147
how upset the PM is.

782
01:11:30.152 --> 01:11:32.780
With respect, the PM
has my direct line.

783
01:11:32.855 --> 01:11:34.392
And he'd have used it...

784
01:11:34.397 --> 01:11:36.397
if he'd wanted
to speak to you.

785
01:11:36.492 --> 01:11:38.960
I'm sorry, M. Things
have changed.

786
01:11:39.561 --> 01:11:42.223
We've had long discussions
with our cousins.

787
01:11:42.331 --> 01:11:44.526
Mr. Greene's interests
and ours now align.

788
01:11:44.633 --> 01:11:47.060
Minister, this man is a
major player in one...

789
01:11:47.065 --> 01:11:49.070
of the most dangerous
organizations...

790
01:11:49.171 --> 01:11:51.135
We've never even heard of.

791
01:11:51.140 --> 01:11:52.974
Foreign policy cannot
be conducted on...

792
01:11:52.979 --> 01:11:54.538
the basis of hunches
and innuendo.

793
01:11:54.543 --> 01:11:56.793
Then give us time
to gather enough evidence...

794
01:11:56.845 --> 01:11:58.845
so you can make
informed decisions.

795
01:11:58.881 --> 01:12:00.881
Fine.

796
01:12:01.383 --> 01:12:04.409
Say you're right.
Say Greene is a villain.

797
01:12:04.520 --> 01:12:06.903
If we refused to do
business with villains,

798
01:12:06.908 --> 01:12:09.014
we'd have almost no
one to trade with.

799
01:12:09.091 --> 01:12:10.745
The world's running
out of oil, M.

800
01:12:10.750 --> 01:12:12.356
The Russians aren't
playing ball.

801
01:12:12.361 --> 01:12:14.725
The Americans and Chinese
are dividing up what's left.

802
01:12:14.730 --> 01:12:17.198
Right or wrong
doesn't come into it.

803
01:12:17.266 --> 01:12:19.666
We're acting out of necessity.

804
01:12:22.570 --> 01:12:24.902
Bond is running wild.

805
01:12:26.207 --> 01:12:28.869
Who's to say he
hasn't been turned?

806
01:12:28.943 --> 01:12:30.055
Pull him in...

807
01:12:30.060 --> 01:12:32.845
or the Americans
will put him down.

808
01:12:36.017 --> 01:12:38.110
I think I found a way out.

809
01:12:39.287 --> 01:12:41.287
You're freezing.

810
01:12:41.856 --> 01:12:43.856
I'm fine.

811
01:12:59.707 --> 01:13:02.642
So what is it that Greene has
that you want?

812
01:13:07.748 --> 01:13:08.791
It's not Greene.

813
01:13:08.796 --> 01:13:11.275
It's Medrano, the
man he met in Haiti.

814
01:13:13.488 --> 01:13:16.321
My father worked for
the military junta.

815
01:13:16.924 --> 01:13:18.924
He was a very cruel man,

816
01:13:20.728 --> 01:13:22.728
but he was my father.

817
01:13:26.334 --> 01:13:28.393
When I was a small child...

818
01:13:28.469 --> 01:13:31.632
the opposition sent general
Medrano to our house.

819
01:13:33.941 --> 01:13:35.941
He shot my father.

820
01:13:36.677 --> 01:13:39.510
He did things to my
mother and my sister...

821
01:13:40.481 --> 01:13:43.348
and then strangled
them while I watched.

822
01:13:45.353 --> 01:13:47.981
I was too young to
be any trouble,

823
01:13:49.323 --> 01:13:51.416
so he just smiled at me...

824
01:13:53.861 --> 01:13:56.022
and set the house on fire.

825
01:13:58.766 --> 01:14:00.766
He left his mark.

826
01:14:04.338 --> 01:14:06.035
So when I pulled
you off the boat...

827
01:14:06.040 --> 01:14:08.440
I waited years
for that chance.

828
01:14:09.677 --> 01:14:11.677
I apologize.

829
01:14:13.781 --> 01:14:15.939
It seems we're both
using Greene...

830
01:14:15.944 --> 01:14:17.944
to get to somebody.

831
01:14:18.152 --> 01:14:20.152
You lost somebody?

832
01:14:20.488 --> 01:14:22.488
I did, yes.

833
01:14:22.857 --> 01:14:24.882
You catch whoever did it?

834
01:14:25.393 --> 01:14:27.393
No. Not yet.

835
01:14:28.896 --> 01:14:30.896
Tell me when you do.

836
01:14:31.532 --> 01:14:33.898
I'd like to know how it feels.

837
01:14:39.073 --> 01:14:41.073
We should go.

838
01:14:41.242 --> 01:14:43.242
You ready?

839
01:15:16.544 --> 01:15:18.603
They used dynamite.

840
01:15:21.515 --> 01:15:23.847
This used to be a riverbed.

841
01:15:40.701 --> 01:15:43.966
Greene isn't after the oil.
He wants the water.

842
01:15:45.272 --> 01:15:46.936
We can't leave it like this.

843
01:15:46.941 --> 01:15:49.407
It's one dam. He's
creating a drought.

844
01:15:49.412 --> 01:15:51.412
He'll have built others.

845
01:17:21.101 --> 01:17:23.365
Excuse me, sir. Your
wife left a message.

846
01:17:23.470 --> 01:17:24.536
The English woman,

847
01:17:24.541 --> 01:17:26.541
she left it for
you this morning.

848
01:17:26.606 --> 01:17:28.606
- Thank you.
- My pleasure.

849
01:17:30.543 --> 01:17:32.543
What is it?

850
01:17:33.179 --> 01:17:35.647
Would you mind
waiting down here?

851
01:17:36.316 --> 01:17:38.316
I'll be outside.

852
01:17:56.970 --> 01:17:58.995
So that's what she meant.

853
01:17:59.405 --> 01:18:00.902
I hope you can
trust these men.

854
01:18:00.907 --> 01:18:03.341
Just a moment. It's Tanner.

855
01:18:04.310 --> 01:18:06.310
Yes?

856
01:18:06.579 --> 01:18:08.042
We've got the girl downstairs.

857
01:18:08.047 --> 01:18:09.363
She says to tell
you she's sorry...

858
01:18:09.368 --> 01:18:10.345
but this is not her fight.

859
01:18:10.350 --> 01:18:12.046
It isn't. Let her go.

860
01:18:12.051 --> 01:18:14.051
She isn't our concern.

861
01:18:14.587 --> 01:18:16.587
Well, I'm disappointed.

862
01:18:16.856 --> 01:18:17.986
You are?

863
01:18:17.991 --> 01:18:20.091
How much oil
did the Americans promise you?

864
01:18:20.193 --> 01:18:21.356
This isn't about oil.

865
01:18:21.361 --> 01:18:23.681
- Well, that's good,
because there isn't any.

866
01:18:23.686 --> 01:18:24.592
It's about trust.

867
01:18:24.597 --> 01:18:26.528
You said you weren't motivated
by revenge.

868
01:18:26.533 --> 01:18:29.024
- I'm motivated by my duty.
- No.

869
01:18:30.036 --> 01:18:33.028
I think you are so blinded
by inconsolable rage...

870
01:18:33.106 --> 01:18:35.506
that you don't
care who you hurt.

871
01:18:35.575 --> 01:18:37.672
When you can't tell
your friends...

872
01:18:37.677 --> 01:18:39.773
from your enemies,
it's time to go.

873
01:18:46.719 --> 01:18:48.808
You might like to tell
her your theory...

874
01:18:48.813 --> 01:18:50.185
about there being no oil.

875
01:18:50.190 --> 01:18:52.283
Her lungs are full of it.

876
01:18:53.693 --> 01:18:56.218
- It was Greene.
- No doubt. But why?

877
01:18:57.730 --> 01:19:00.893
- It's just misdirection.
- I mean, why her, Bond?

878
01:19:00.967 --> 01:19:03.344
She was just supposed
to send you home.

879
01:19:03.349 --> 01:19:06.030
She worked in an office,
collecting reports.

880
01:19:06.539 --> 01:19:09.235
Look how well your
charm works, James.

881
01:19:09.542 --> 01:19:12.375
They'll do anything
for you, won't they?

882
01:19:12.612 --> 01:19:14.612
How many is that now?

883
01:19:15.148 --> 01:19:17.399
You're removed from
duty and suspended...

884
01:19:17.404 --> 01:19:19.113
pending further investigation.

885
01:19:19.118 --> 01:19:21.521
You'll give whatever
weapons you have...

886
01:19:21.526 --> 01:19:23.748
to these men and
leave with them now.

887
01:20:08.701 --> 01:20:10.701
Miss Fields showed
true bravery.

888
01:20:10.803 --> 01:20:12.803
I want that mentioned
in your report.

889
01:20:12.805 --> 01:20:14.776
- Now you and I need
to see this through.

890
01:20:14.781 --> 01:20:15.837
There's nowhere to go.

891
01:20:15.842 --> 01:20:18.811
There's a capture or
kill order out on you.

892
01:20:19.512 --> 01:20:21.605
Who would have done that?

893
01:20:30.456 --> 01:20:32.456
- Ma'am?
- Find out where he's going.

894
01:20:32.458 --> 01:20:33.351
- He's on to something.

895
01:20:33.356 --> 01:20:34.522
Ma'am, the CIA is insisting...

896
01:20:34.527 --> 01:20:35.981
I could give a shit
about the CIA...

897
01:20:35.986 --> 01:20:37.157
or their trumped-up evidence.

898
01:20:37.162 --> 01:20:40.154
He's my agent, and
I trust him. Go on.

899
01:20:52.577 --> 01:20:53.189
- Get in.

900
01:20:53.194 --> 01:20:55.307
Are you gonna
try and shoot me?

901
01:20:55.380 --> 01:20:57.380
I said, get in.

902
01:21:11.596 --> 01:21:14.156
You're gonna get botulism
if you keep drinking that.

903
01:21:14.232 --> 01:21:16.232
It's bottled water.

904
01:21:17.169 --> 01:21:18.644
It probably came
from some stream...

905
01:21:18.649 --> 01:21:20.000
just around the
corner from here.

906
01:21:20.005 --> 01:21:22.530
Bunch of little
kids peeing in it.

907
01:21:23.709 --> 01:21:25.238
That's why I eat the peppers.

908
01:21:25.243 --> 01:21:27.218
Well, all I'm saying is...

909
01:21:27.223 --> 01:21:30.340
you can't trust a damn
thing around here.

910
01:21:36.688 --> 01:21:37.155
You know,

911
01:21:37.160 --> 01:21:39.160
you should just
answer, 'CIA,' Felix.

912
01:21:39.191 --> 01:21:41.489
A taxi driver told me
where the office was.

913
01:21:41.560 --> 01:21:43.938
Well, if we're so
easy to find, James,

914
01:21:43.943 --> 01:21:45.943
you really should come visit.

915
01:21:46.865 --> 01:21:50.494
Or maybe you should come out
and see some more of the city.

916
01:22:10.455 --> 01:22:12.455
I heard a rumor
you'd gone native.

917
01:22:12.457 --> 01:22:14.457
Felix.

918
01:22:18.897 --> 01:22:19.993
You know, I was
just wondering...

919
01:22:19.998 --> 01:22:21.228
what South America
would look like...

920
01:22:21.233 --> 01:22:23.463
if nobody gave a damn
about coke or communism.

921
01:22:23.468 --> 01:22:24.798
It's always impressed
me the way...

922
01:22:24.803 --> 01:22:26.133
you boys have carved
this place up.

923
01:22:26.138 --> 01:22:29.266
I'll take that as a compliment
coming from a Brit.

924
01:22:30.809 --> 01:22:33.903
Are you sure you're playing
with the right side?

925
01:22:33.979 --> 01:22:35.979
Regimes change once
a week down here.

926
01:22:35.981 --> 01:22:37.944
Medrano'll be no dirtier
than the next guy.

927
01:22:37.949 --> 01:22:40.080
Oh, you see, that's what I
like about U.S. intelligence.

928
01:22:40.085 --> 01:22:41.581
You'll lie down with anybody.

929
01:22:41.586 --> 01:22:43.986
Including you, brother.
Including you.

930
01:22:44.089 --> 01:22:46.489
Do you know you're
being played?

931
01:22:46.591 --> 01:22:48.422
Dominic Greene's gonna
suck this place dry,

932
01:22:48.427 --> 01:22:49.956
and then he's gonna move on,
and you're gonna be left...

933
01:22:49.961 --> 01:22:51.291
picking up the
broken crockery.

934
01:22:51.296 --> 01:22:52.294
What can I tell you?

935
01:22:52.299 --> 01:22:54.261
There's no such thing
as a free lunch.

936
01:22:54.266 --> 01:22:54.962
Well, you see, Felix.

937
01:22:54.967 --> 01:22:56.263
I don't think you're
half as cynical...

938
01:22:56.268 --> 01:22:57.464
as you make out to be.

939
01:22:57.469 --> 01:22:59.469
You don't know me.

940
01:23:01.773 --> 01:23:04.640
Why? Just because you
didn't come alone?

941
01:23:05.277 --> 01:23:07.745
- How long have I got?
- Thirty seconds.

942
01:23:09.614 --> 01:23:12.913
Well, that doesn't give us
a lot of time, does it?

943
01:23:13.952 --> 01:23:15.943
Medrano can't move
until he pays off...

944
01:23:15.948 --> 01:23:17.584
the army and the police chief.

945
01:23:17.589 --> 01:23:19.286
Greene's bringing
him his money now.

946
01:23:19.291 --> 01:23:21.657
A hotel called La
Perla de las Dunas...

947
01:23:21.760 --> 01:23:23.760
in the desert.

948
01:23:23.829 --> 01:23:25.525
Thank you, Felix.

949
01:23:25.530 --> 01:23:27.623
James, move your ass.

950
01:23:28.800 --> 01:23:30.800
Get down. Get down, now.

951
01:23:45.817 --> 01:23:47.817
Move it. Move it.

952
01:23:53.625 --> 01:23:56.321
What the hell happened?
What did you tell him?

953
01:23:56.394 --> 01:23:58.394
Just what we agreed.

954
01:25:22.279 --> 01:25:24.279
What are you doing?

955
01:25:25.916 --> 01:25:27.916
The slide's caught.

956
01:25:28.752 --> 01:25:31.050
Maybe you should
check your own.

957
01:25:31.121 --> 01:25:33.121
I will.

958
01:25:37.494 --> 01:25:39.724
Have you ever killed someone?

959
01:25:43.000 --> 01:25:44.269
Your training will
tell you that...

960
01:25:44.274 --> 01:25:45.397
when the adrenaline
kicks in...

961
01:25:45.402 --> 01:25:47.402
you should compensate.

962
01:25:48.272 --> 01:25:50.472
But part of you is
not gonna believe...

963
01:25:50.477 --> 01:25:52.902
the training because
this kill is personal.

964
01:25:53.644 --> 01:25:55.644
Take a deep breath.

965
01:25:55.813 --> 01:25:57.643
You only need one shot.

966
01:25:57.648 --> 01:25:59.648
Make it count.

967
01:27:06.216 --> 01:27:08.216
In euros,

968
01:27:08.485 --> 01:27:09.982
as requested.

969
01:27:09.987 --> 01:27:12.615
The dollar isn't
what it once was.

970
01:27:13.657 --> 01:27:15.657
The cost of war.

971
01:27:17.127 --> 01:27:18.581
I am afraid that
the corruption...

972
01:27:18.586 --> 01:27:19.825
in this current government...

973
01:27:19.830 --> 01:27:22.060
can no longer be tolerated.

974
01:27:24.868 --> 01:27:26.868
And mine?

975
01:27:26.870 --> 01:27:29.532
Right after you
sign over my land.

976
01:27:45.189 --> 01:27:47.189
My first official act.

977
01:27:52.596 --> 01:27:54.860
And this, if you would.

978
01:27:54.932 --> 01:27:56.362
What is this?

979
01:27:56.367 --> 01:27:57.596
As of this moment,

980
01:27:57.601 --> 01:27:59.422
my organization owns...

981
01:27:59.427 --> 01:28:02.595
more than 60% of
Bolivia's water supply.

982
01:28:02.706 --> 01:28:06.369
So this contract states
that your new government...

983
01:28:06.443 --> 01:28:09.378
will use us as
utilities provider.

984
01:28:10.180 --> 01:28:13.115
This is double what
we are paying now.

985
01:28:16.687 --> 01:28:18.882
Well, then don't sign it.

986
01:28:19.623 --> 01:28:21.783
But you should
know something...

987
01:28:21.788 --> 01:28:24.219
about me and the
people I work with.

988
01:28:25.362 --> 01:28:27.387
We deal with the
left or the right,

989
01:28:27.464 --> 01:28:31.093
with dictators or liberators.

990
01:28:31.735 --> 01:28:34.363
If the current president
had been more agreeable.

991
01:28:34.438 --> 01:28:36.633
I wouldn't be talking to you.

992
01:28:36.740 --> 01:28:38.970
So, if you decide not to sign,

993
01:28:39.076 --> 01:28:39.904
you will wake up...

994
01:28:39.909 --> 01:28:41.306
with your balls
in your mouth...

995
01:28:41.311 --> 01:28:44.644
and your willing replacement
standing over you.

996
01:28:46.483 --> 01:28:48.781
If you doubt that,
then shoot me,

997
01:28:48.886 --> 01:28:52.116
take that money
and have a good night's sleep.

998
01:29:52.482 --> 01:29:54.950
You and I had a mutual friend.

999
01:32:44.987 --> 01:32:47.922
Sounds like you just
lost another one.

1000
01:33:57.392 --> 01:33:59.587
Not this way. Not this way.

1001
01:34:00.228 --> 01:34:02.228
I can't. I can't.

1002
01:34:13.408 --> 01:34:15.408
Come here.

1003
01:34:19.848 --> 01:34:21.711
Like you said,

1004
01:34:21.716 --> 01:34:23.716
'Take a deep breath.

1005
01:34:24.853 --> 01:34:26.853
'Make it count.'

1006
01:34:32.594 --> 01:34:34.594
Close your eyes.

1007
01:34:42.871 --> 01:34:44.871
Come on.

1008
01:34:58.720 --> 01:35:00.720
Wait here.

1009
01:35:32.153 --> 01:35:34.951
- You promised that you'd...
- Let you go?

1010
01:35:35.490 --> 01:35:37.822
I answered your questions.

1011
01:35:37.926 --> 01:35:40.656
I told you what you wanted
to know about Quantum.

1012
01:35:40.762 --> 01:35:42.659
Yes, you did,

1013
01:35:42.664 --> 01:35:44.110
and your friends'd
know that...

1014
01:35:44.115 --> 01:35:45.795
so they're probably
looking for you.

1015
01:35:45.800 --> 01:35:47.209
But the good news is,

1016
01:35:47.214 --> 01:35:49.429
you're in the
middle of a desert.

1017
01:35:53.174 --> 01:35:55.174
Here.

1018
01:35:56.344 --> 01:35:58.689
I bet you make it 20
miles before you...

1019
01:35:58.694 --> 01:36:00.143
consider drinking that.

1020
01:36:00.148 --> 01:36:02.148
Goodbye, Mr. Greene.

1021
01:36:41.723 --> 01:36:43.723
Thank you.

1022
01:36:43.925 --> 01:36:45.925
It's my pleasure.

1023
01:36:47.028 --> 01:36:49.028
Are you all right?

1024
01:36:49.063 --> 01:36:50.727
Fine.

1025
01:36:50.732 --> 01:36:53.064
But I keep thinking,
'He's dead.

1026
01:36:53.501 --> 01:36:55.331
'Now what?'

1027
01:36:55.336 --> 01:36:57.770
Well, the dam we saw
will have to come down,

1028
01:36:57.872 --> 01:36:59.002
and there'll be others, too.

1029
01:36:59.007 --> 01:37:01.874
Someone who worked for Greene
might be of help.

1030
01:37:02.744 --> 01:37:04.744
Not a bad idea.

1031
01:37:09.182 --> 01:37:12.083
Do you think they'll
be able to sleep now?

1032
01:37:14.454 --> 01:37:17.446
I don't think the dead
care about vengeance.

1033
01:37:19.893 --> 01:37:22.088
I wish I could set you free.

1034
01:37:26.533 --> 01:37:28.694
But your prison is in there.

1035
01:38:19.987 --> 01:38:22.421
Fine. Anything
for an easy life.

1036
01:38:25.926 --> 01:38:27.926
Sit down.

1037
01:38:28.061 --> 01:38:30.061
Sit down.

1038
01:38:30.764 --> 01:38:32.764
It's okay, baby.

1039
01:38:49.182 --> 01:38:51.182
You're Canadian?

1040
01:38:51.351 --> 01:38:53.751
You work in Canadian
intelligence?

1041
01:38:53.820 --> 01:38:56.015
It's all right. I know you do.

1042
01:38:56.523 --> 01:38:58.487
And knowing this man.

1043
01:38:58.492 --> 01:38:59.678
I'd guess you have access...

1044
01:38:59.683 --> 01:39:01.123
to some very
sensitive material...

1045
01:39:01.128 --> 01:39:03.187
which you're gonna be
forced to give up.

1046
01:39:03.296 --> 01:39:04.526
His life will be threatened,

1047
01:39:04.531 --> 01:39:07.500
and because you love him,
you won't hesitate.

1048
01:39:08.468 --> 01:39:10.468
It's a beautiful necklace.

1049
01:39:11.171 --> 01:39:13.171
Did he give it to you?

1050
01:39:15.008 --> 01:39:17.203
I have one just like it.

1051
01:39:20.047 --> 01:39:22.515
He gave it to a
friend of mine,

1052
01:39:22.616 --> 01:39:24.616
someone very close to me.

1053
01:39:28.321 --> 01:39:29.718
Your name is?

1054
01:39:29.723 --> 01:39:31.723
- Corrine.
- Corrine.

1055
01:39:32.059 --> 01:39:33.655
Corrine, I suggest
you leave now.

1056
01:39:33.660 --> 01:39:34.622
You contact your people,

1057
01:39:34.627 --> 01:39:36.191
and you tell them to
check their seals.

1058
01:39:36.196 --> 01:39:38.126
They have a leak.

1059
01:39:38.131 --> 01:39:40.131
Do it now, please.

1060
01:39:40.834 --> 01:39:43.860
This man and I have
some unfinished business.

1061
01:39:54.514 --> 01:39:56.514
Thank you.

1062
01:40:00.554 --> 01:40:02.517
Please.

1063
01:40:02.522 --> 01:40:04.522
Make it quick.

1064
01:40:13.433 --> 01:40:14.996
Is he still alive?

1065
01:40:15.001 --> 01:40:16.698
He is.

1066
01:40:16.703 --> 01:40:18.703
I'm surprised.

1067
01:40:19.439 --> 01:40:21.369
Did you find what
you were looking for?

1068
01:40:21.374 --> 01:40:23.374
- Yes.
- Good.

1069
01:40:24.211 --> 01:40:26.568
- I assume you
have no regrets.

1070
01:40:26.573 --> 01:40:27.242
I don't.

1071
01:40:27.247 --> 01:40:29.247
What about you?

1072
01:40:29.349 --> 01:40:32.250
Of course not.
That would be unprofessional.

1073
01:40:33.220 --> 01:40:34.382
They found Greene dead...

1074
01:40:34.387 --> 01:40:36.365
in the middle of
the Bolivian desert,

1075
01:40:36.370 --> 01:40:37.219
of all places.

1076
01:40:37.224 --> 01:40:39.624
Two bullets in the
back of his skull.

1077
01:40:39.726 --> 01:40:42.422
They found motor
oil in his stomach.

1078
01:40:42.529 --> 01:40:44.529
Does that mean
anything to you?

1079
01:40:44.564 --> 01:40:46.261
Wish I could help.

1080
01:40:46.266 --> 01:40:48.072
You'll be glad to
know, I straightened...

1081
01:40:48.077 --> 01:40:49.397
things out with the Americans.

1082
01:40:49.402 --> 01:40:51.366
Your friend Leiter's
been promoted.

1083
01:40:51.371 --> 01:40:52.801
He replaced Beam.

1084
01:40:52.806 --> 01:40:55.274
Well, then the right
people kept their jobs.

1085
01:40:55.375 --> 01:40:57.375
Something like that.

1086
01:40:58.645 --> 01:41:01.205
Congratulations.
You were right.

1087
01:41:01.281 --> 01:41:03.281
About what?

1088
01:41:03.283 --> 01:41:05.283
About Vesper.

1089
01:41:07.254 --> 01:41:09.254
Ma'am.

1090
01:41:10.891 --> 01:41:12.891
Bond.

1091
01:41:13.493 --> 01:41:15.493
I need you back.

1092
01:41:15.629 --> 01:41:17.629
I never left.

1093
01:44:08.241 --> 01:44:14.241
<font color=#38B0DE>Subtitles
by ElDorado80</font>
